  Compile-time assertion: var _ DLQPublisher = (*MQTTDLQPublisher)(nil)

Check 2 — Manual-ack contract documentation (mqtt.go:224-236).
  Quoted verbatim:
    "PipelineSubscriber relies on bounded MQTT redelivery: when the pipeline
     returns ErrPayloadDrop AND the message has not yet hit MaxRedeliveries,
     the handler returns WITHOUT calling msg.Ack(), expecting the broker to
     redeliver at the next retry. For this to work the underlying paho client
     MUST be constructed with SetAutoAckDisabled(true) (Paho v3 wire-default
     is auto-ack AFTER the handler returns, which would silently break the
     redelivery contract). The legacy NewClient constructor in this package
     does NOT set that option because the legacy subscriber depends on
     auto-ack semantics; the caller wiring PipelineSubscriber into
     cmd/<server>/main.go is responsible for constructing a separate paho
     client with SetAutoAckDisabled(true) before passing it in.
     NewPipelineSubscriber documents but does not validate this requirement
     (paho exposes no read-back for the option)."

Check 3 — handlePayload + handlePipelineError ack/nack tree (mqtt.go:672-805).
  - Line 678 (msg.Ack): topic-parse failure → ack-and-drop.
  - Line 689 (msg.Ack): ErrUnknownVIN → ack-and-drop.
  - Line 697-698 (NO ack): VIN resolver infra failure → broker redelivers.
  - Line 707 (msg.Ack): pipeline returns nil → ack.
  - Line 727 (NO ack): context.Canceled / DeadlineExceeded → no DLQ either.
  - Line 744 (NO ack): codec drop below MaxRedeliveries → broker redelivers.
  - Line 791-792 (NO ack): codec drop AT/over MaxRedeliveries but DLQ
    publish failed → broker redelivers AND the next pass retries DLQ.
  - Line 804 (msg.Ack): codec drop AT/over MaxRedeliveries AND DLQ publish
    succeeded → poison-pill durably captured, ack.
  - Line 752 (NO ack): non-retriable infra error → no DLQ either.
  All four branches that DO NOT ack rely on broker redelivery — which only
  works if the underlying paho client was constructed with
  SetAutoAckDisabled(true). Without it paho auto-acks AFTER handlePayload
  returns regardless of whether msg.Ack() was called.

Check 4 — Existing legacy NewClient as anti-pattern (mqtt.go:34-71).
  Legacy NewClient sets SetCleanSession(true) + SetAutoReconnect(true) and
  does NOT set SetAutoAckDisabled. Manual-ack contract block above explicitly
  notes this is intentional for the legacy subscriber. The new helper must
  NOT reuse NewClient as a base; it builds its own ClientOptions from
  pahomqtt.NewClientOptions() per Decision #2.

