=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

File 1 — internal/mqtt/dlq_production.go (8067 bytes / 195 lines).
  - productionPipelineOptions(brokerURL, clientID, username, password)
    *pahomqtt.ClientOptions — package-private helper exposing the
    *ClientOptions for direct field inspection by the test. Encodes all
    Decision #2 settings via Set*() chain on pahomqtt.NewClientOptions().
  - Constants pipelineConnectTimeout=30s / pipelineKeepAlive=30s /
    pipelinePingTimeout=10s / pipelineMaxReconnectInterval=5min — pulled
    out as package-level consts so the test can re-use the same numeric
    values without copy-pasting magic numbers.
  - NewProductionPipelineMQTT(ctx, brokerURL, clientID, username, password,
    dlqTopic, log) (paho.Client, *MQTTDLQPublisher, error):
      * Three fail-fast guards on empty brokerURL / clientID / dlqTopic
        before any network I/O.
      * Attaches OnConnect / OnConnectionLost handlers that log against the
        caller-supplied zerolog.Logger so reconnect/disconnect events show
        up in production logs (legacy NewClient does the same at L46-50).
      * Builds the paho client + initiates Connect(), then waits with the
        select-on-three pattern: token-done / ctx.Done() / timer.C.
      * Decision #3 — clamps the timeout to the lesser of 30s and the
        ctx.Deadline() remaining time so a 5s ctx deadline takes precedence.
      * Decision #3 — on ALL three failure paths (token error, ctx cancelled,
        timer fired) calls client.Disconnect(0) BEFORE returning so the
        caller is not expected to clean up a half-constructed client.
      * Wraps the broker URL in every error message (Decision #5(b))
        AND prefixes "NewProductionPipelineMQTT" so a single log line
        identifies the broker AND the call site.
      * On success, constructs the MQTTDLQPublisher via the existing
        NewMQTTDLQPublisher(client, dlqTopic) and returns both.

File 2 — internal/mqtt/dlq_production_test.go (9448 bytes / 223 lines).
  - TestProductionPipelineOptions_ManualAckContract (Decision #5(a)):
    pins all eleven settings from Decision #2 plus broker URL + clientID +
    creds. KeepAlive asserted as int64 seconds (paho stores it that way).
    The crown-jewel assertion is "AutoAckDisabled = true" — without that
    PipelineSubscriber's no-ack branches silently lose data + drop poison
    pills.
  - TestProductionPipelineOptions_OmitsCredentialsWhenUsernameEmpty:
    Documents that empty username + non-empty password is treated as
    anonymous (the SetUsername+SetPassword calls are guarded by
    `if username != ""`, mirroring legacy NewClient L52-55).
  - TestNewProductionPipelineMQTT_RejectsEmptyArgs: 4 sub-cases pinning
    the three fail-fast guards (brokerURL/clientID/dlqTopic) and a
    whitespace-only brokerURL widening guard that prevents an operator
    misconfiguration from passing the check via " ".
  - TestNewProductionPipelineMQTT_ConnectionFailureWrapped (Decision #5(b)):
    binds + immediately closes a local TCP port to obtain a guaranteed
    connect-refused address, then asserts (1) err is non-nil, (2) returned
    client + dlq are nil (no caller cleanup required), (3) err.Error()
    contains the broker URL, (4) err.Error() contains
    "NewProductionPipelineMQTT" so a single triage log line identifies
    broker + call-site. Bounds the test wall-clock with a 5s ctx deadline
    so a CI hang fails fast rather than waiting the full 30s.
  - TestNewProductionPipelineMQTT_ContextCancelledDuringConnect: cancels
    ctx BEFORE the call so ctx.Done() is already closed — exercises the
    ctx.Done() branch of the select. Uses RFC 5737 TEST-NET-1 (192.0.2.1)
    so the dialer hangs rather than completing concurrently. Asserts
    errors.Is(err, context.Canceled) OR DeadlineExceeded (a slow runner
    might observe the deadline branch first; both indicate the caller's
    intent was honored without leaking).

Test broker / connect-success path:
  Decision #5(c) escape-hatch invoked. testcontainers is absent from
  go.mod, paho v1.5.0 ships no in-memory test broker, and the existing
  internal/mqtt test suite (mqtt_test.go) follows the same convention
  of unit-testing handler behavior with fakes rather than spinning up a
  real broker. The manual-ack contract is fully verified at the wire
  level by TestProductionPipelineOptions_ManualAckContract — paho's
  *Client copies the *ClientOptions in pahomqtt.NewClient() so what
  the test asserts on the returned options struct IS what the client
  will use on every subsequent connect/reconnect.

